<title>HUNGARY: Hungary March net household savings up HUF29.6 bln.</title>
<headline>Hungary March net household savings up HUF29.6 bln.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungary's net household savings rose 29.6 billion forints in March to 2,533.9 billion forints, the National Bank of Hungary (NBH) said on Monday.</p>
<p>    (in billion forints)    March '97     Feb '97     March 96</p>
<p>    Forint savings	    2,387.0	 2,357.0     1,861.1</p>
<p>    Foreign currency	    474.6	   478.6	 455.4</p>
<p>    Total savings	     2,861.6	 2,835.6     2,316.5</p>
<p>    Total loans		   327.7	   331.3	 360.5</p>
<p>    Net household savings   2,533.9	 2,504.3     1,956.0</p>
<p>NOTE - The NBH said that net household savings rose by 122.5 billion forints in the first quarter of the year, down from an increase of 133.5 billion forints in the same period of 1996. The figures are not inflation-adjusted. March 1997 figures are preliminary. Consumer price inflation was 18.8 percent year-on-year in March.</p>
<p>($1 = 182.25 forints)</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327 4042</p>
